{"id":"B2-L167","title":"Criticism or regret (should have, shouldn’t have) — use","cefr":"B2","level":"B2","unit":"B2-U10","focus":"Crítica ou arrependimento (should have, shouldn’t have) — uso","targets":{"grammar":"Crítica ou arrependimento (should have, shouldn’t have) — uso","pron":"Acento para enfatizar informação","verbs":[],"pv":[],"expr":[],"words":["ruined sample","overnight exposure","unlabelled tube","refrigerated storage","double-check","lab mishap","clean-up protocol","checklist habit","ink marker","sample rack","spoiled culture","incubator","sterile technique","lab notebook entry","apology to team","lessons from failure","story setting","inner thought","quiet lab","dim corridor"],"field":"Ciência","genre":"Conto e trecho de peça","skill":"Leitura","words_min":20},"frames":[{"tag":"Abertura","title":"Lesson 167 · Criticism or regret (should have, shouldn’t have) — use","blocks":[{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Nesta aula","body":["**Foco:** Crítica ou arrependimento (should have, shouldn’t have) — uso.","**Pronúncia:** Acento para enfatizar informação.","**20 palavras novas** (ciência).","**Texto do dia:** conto e trecho de peça."]},{"type":"p","t":"**Objetivo de comunicação (B2):** eu consigo usar should have e shouldn’t have para refletir sobre erros num conto de laboratório."},{"type":"box","kind":"exam","t":"Ponte para as provas","body":["","Esta aula treina **ler textos curtos e achar informação (IELTS Reading, TOEFL Reading)**."]}]},{"tag":"Aquecimento","title":"Warm-up · Say the words","blocks":[{"type":"p","t":"Toque em 🔊, ouça e repita cada palavra. Depois tente adivinhar o sentido."},{"type":"words","items":[["ruined sample","amostra arruinada"],["overnight exposure","exposição noturna"],["unlabelled tube","tubo sem etiqueta"],["refrigerated storage","armazenamento refrigerado"],["double-check","conferir duas vezes"],["lab mishap","acidente de laboratório"],["clean-up protocol","protocolo de limpeza"],["checklist habit","hábito de lista de verificação"],["ink marker","marcador de tinta"],["sample rack","suporte de amostras"],["spoiled culture","cultura estragada"],["incubator","incubadora"],["sterile technique","técnica estéril"],["lab notebook entry","anotação no caderno"],["apology to team","desculpa à equipe"],["lessons from failure","lições do fracasso"],["story setting","cenário da história"],["inner thought","pensamento íntimo"],["quiet lab","laboratório silencioso"],["dim corridor","corredor escuro"]]}]},{"tag":"Leitura","title":"Reading · A short story","blocks":[{"type":"text","title":"Short Story: The Spoiled Sample","paras":["Dr. Neves stared at the ruined sample. “I **should have labeled** the tubes,” she said. “I **shouldn’t have left** them out overnight.” Her assistant **ought to have reminded** her, but he had gone home.","She **shouldn’t have blamed** him. “It’s my fault,” she admitted, and wrote a new plan: label, refrigerate and double-check."],"kicker":"STORY","by":"Short Fiction Club","gloss":[["ruined","arruinado"],["label","etiquetar"],["fault","culpa"],["refrigerate","refrigerar"]]}]},{"tag":"Compreensão","title":"Did you understand?","blocks":[{"type":"tfng","title":"","items":[{"q":"Dr. Neves left the tubes out overnight.","ans":"T","why":"left them out."},{"q":"Her assistant stayed late to remind her.","ans":"F","why":"had gone home."},{"q":"She wrote a new plan.","ans":"T","why":"new plan."}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Vocabulary in context","items":[{"q":"“label” (verbo) = ?","opts":["etiquetar","lábio","lavar"],"ans":0,"why":"label."},{"q":"“fault” = ?","opts":["culpa","falta só","falso"],"ans":0,"why":"fault."}]}]},{"tag":"Gramática","title":"should have × shouldn’t have — uso","blocks":[{"type":"table","head":["Situação","Frase"],"rows":[["faltou fazer","I **should have labeled** the tubes."],["fez algo errado","I **shouldn’t have left** them out."],["crítica a outro","He **ought to have reminded** me."],["auto-perdão","It **can’t have been** easy."]],"cap":"should have × shouldn’t have — uso"},{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Regra","body":"Use **should have** para ações **que faltaram** e **shouldn’t have** para ações **que não deveriam ter ocorrido**. Em crítica a outros, o tom pode ser forte: suavize com *perhaps* ou *might have*."}]},{"tag":"Prática","title":"Practice","blocks":[{"type":"gap","title":"Complete the sentences","bank":null,"items":[{"s":"I ___ have labeled the tubes. (should)","a":"should","why":"should have."},{"s":"I ___ have left them out overnight. (shouldn’t)","a":"shouldn’t","why":"shouldn’t have."},{"s":"He ought to have ___ me. (remind, part.)","a":"reminded","why":"particípio."},{"s":"She wrote a new ___ . (plan)","a":"plan","why":"substantivo."}]},{"type":"match","title":"Match the word to its meaning","pairs":[["ruined sample","amostra arruinada"],["overnight exposure","exposição noturna"],["unlabelled tube","tubo sem etiqueta"],["lab assistant","assistente de laboratório"],["refrigerated storage","armazenamento refrigerado"]]},{"type":"order","title":"Put the words in order","items":[{"words":["went","wrong","with","the","sample","What"],"ans":"What went wrong with the sample","pt":"O que deu errado com a amostra?"},{"words":["shouldn't","she","have","done","And","what"],"ans":"And what shouldn't she have done","pt":"E o que ela não deveria ter feito?"}]}]},{"tag":"Vocabulário","title":"Words and expressions","blocks":[{"type":"vocab","items":[{"w":"ruined sample","pos":"word","pt":"amostra arruinada","ex":"Ruined sample.","expt":"Amostra arruinada."},{"w":"overnight exposure","pos":"word","pt":"exposição noturna","ex":"Overnight exposure.","expt":"Exposição noturna."},{"w":"unlabelled tube","pos":"word","pt":"tubo sem etiqueta","ex":"Unlabelled tube.","expt":"Tubo sem etiqueta."},{"w":"refrigerated storage","pos":"word","pt":"armazenamento refrigerado","ex":"Refrigerated storage.","expt":"Armazenamento refrigerado."},{"w":"double-check","pos":"word","pt":"conferir duas vezes","ex":"Double-check.","expt":